=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  - Data sources (web useTranslation + useUnits): bound through the P1/S8 seam
    VehicleGaugesSource→VehicleGaugesModel. No HTTP in the view; the snapshot carries the
    Vehicle (model) + VehicleState slice + the useUnits prefs (distance/speed/locale/precision)
    + the load/connection axis.
  - Composition (web TeslaCarViz + RadialGauge×4 + MetricBar + chips):
      • TeslaCarViz -> VehicleCarVizView: ambient glow (sentry>charging>driving>idle), a
        per-model Shape silhouette (sedan/SUV/Cybertruck wedge), spinning 5-spoke wheels
        (driving, Reduce-Motion honoured), battery bar + "NN%", charging bolt + lock badge.
        The atomic TeslaCarViz's shared native peer is owned by the P4 component-library
        bundle (out of scope, not yet present), so it is reproduced scoped to this surface —
        same disposition predecessors use for shared primitives.
      • RadialGauge×4 -> Battery(%, batteryColor) · Range(dist, cyan) · Speed(spd, purple|dark)
        · Power(kW, success|muted). clamp(value,0,max); centre = fmtNumber(clamped, isInteger?0:2);
        arc fills clamped/max. Range/Speed pre-round via Math.round; SI ceilings (600mi / 250mph /
        100mi-per-h) converted through the pref so the fill is unit-invariant.
      • MetricBar -> Battery Level · Estimated Range · (Charge Rate only when is_charging).
        fill = min(value/max,1); sublabels = fmtNumber(level,0)%, formatDistance(rated_range),
        formatDistance(charge_rate)+"/h" (charge_rate is SI m/h).
      • chips -> Lock(green|red) · Sentry(red|muted) · Climate(cyan|muted) · Software(purple,
        "N/A" fallback). Neutral glass pill; only the icon is tinted (web parity).
  - States (ALL rendered, each with a #if DEBUG preview + a model/projection unit test):
      content (=the web source, always-content) · loading (skeleton) · empty (friendly, never
      blank) · error (retry) · stale (freshness chip + "gauges may be stale" banner +
      one-shot auto-refresh) · offline (cached + offline chip + banner). The leaf load/freshness
      states are the sanctioned P4 addition over the pure web component (HeroGauges precedent).
  - i18n (P1/S10): web keys preserved verbatim — common.battery/range/speed/power/batteryLevel/
    estimatedRange/chargeRate + common.locked/unlocked/sentryOn/sentryOff/climateOn/climateOff +
    the common.notAvailable ("N/A") software fallback; native chrome namespaced vehicleGauges.*.
    Every code-referenced key is declared in VehicleGauges.strings (referenced==declared verified,
    0 drift); NO English string literals in native code (all via the facade + Text(verbatim:)).
  - Accessibility: VoiceOver labels on the gauge grid (combined summary), each gauge, each metric
    bar, each chip, the car visualization (battery + active flags), and the freshness chip;
    Dynamic-Type system fonts (Font.TS); Reduce-Motion honoured (gauge arc, bar fill, wheel spin,
    TSFadeIn, TSSkeleton).
  - Telemetry (P1/S11): VehicleGaugesModel.start() emits view.opened with surface slug
    "VehicleGauges" exactly once (OSLog default; prod app injects the shared diagnostics adapter).

